  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "getSSCertificateFingerprint",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/tls.c",
    "description": "Heap-buffer-overflow in TLS certificate fingerprint parsing: getSSCertificateFingerprint reads a 16-bit length from packet->payload[flow->l4.tcp.tls_record_offset+7] after only checking payload_packet_len > tls_record_offset+7. This permits a 2-byte read starting at the last valid byte (needs +8 bound), causing out-of-bounds read at line ~906. Crash occurs in getSSCertificateFingerprint, and it is reached via tlsDetectProtocolFromCertificate/ndpi_search_tls_tcp_udp.",
    "conditions": "In fuzz_process_packet, crafted short/truncated TLS-like TCP payload drives execution into getSSCertificateFingerprint with tls_srv_cert_fingerprint_processed unset and flow->l4.tcp.tls_record_offset near end of payload. The non-certificate handshake branch executes and dereferences *(u_int16_t*)&payload[offset+7] without ensuring two bytes are available (offset+8 < payload_packet_len), triggering OOB read."
  },
